So the test expects after pressing ArrowDown (first down?) that aria-activedescendant on #store equals "autoCompleteJS_result_0". But observed value was "Market Street". That suggests that currently aria-activedescendant is being set to the text content of the selected item rather than its ID.

Looking at the code: In navigationController.js, the update function sets:

config.inputField.setAttribute("aria-activedescendant", list[currentFocus].dataset.value);

Where dataset.value comes from the item creation: In components/Item.js, we set:

result.setAttribute("data-value", item.value[item.key]);

Thus dataset.value holds the actual value (the store name), e.g., "Market Street". However the test expects the aria-activedescendant to be the ID of the option element, like "autoCompleteJS_result_0". According to ARIA spec for combobox with listbox, aria-activedescendant should refer to the ID of the active descendant element (the option). So we need to set aria-activedescendant to the element's ID, not its data-value.

Thus fix: In navigationController.js update function, set attribute to list[currentFocus].id instead of dataset.value.

